{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "DenyHTTP",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::confidential-data",
        "arn:aws:s3:::confidential-data/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

If a user sends an HTTP request, the condition evaluates to true, and the explicit deny kicks in, returning a 403 Forbidden. For encryption at rest, enable default encryption on the bucket (SSE‑S3 or SSE‑KMS) and optionally add a deny statement for `s3:PutObject` where `s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption` header is absent.
